name: truthgraph-context
description: Investigate implementations and plan code changes using TruthGraph search, impact and service/contract evidence. Use for locating code, tracing propagation and reviewing affected callers; repository onboarding requires an explicit request.
metadata:
  version: "2026.10.30.1"
  updated: "2026-10-30"
---

# TruthGraph context

Guidance **2026.10.30.1**, customer MCP **`truthgraph_customer`**. Reuse known IDs/commits. [operator.md](references/operator.md) covers authorized operator work.

## Route the unresolved question

| Task | Preferred operation |
| --- | --- |
| Unknown implementation | `truthgraph_search`, short question, `mode:"hybrid"`, limit 3–5 |
| Known subject/neighbors | `truthgraph_context`, `intent:"lookup"`, limit 3 |
| Explain local implementation | `truthgraph_context`, `intent:"bundle"`, limit 5 |
| Change/callers/propagation | `truthgraph_context`, `intent:"impact"`, actual symbol/contract |
| Service/contract wiring | `truthgraph_context`, `intent:"ownership"`, limit 8 |
| Observed execution | `truthgraph_context`, `intent:"runtime"`, limit 5 |

For changes, request actual symbol/contract impact early; start from the existing handler/serializer for proposed fields. Bundle is not dependency traversal. Use ownership for unresolved wiring. Explain skipped impact through concrete gaps or established facts; avoid checklist calls.

## Establish the source once

Call `truthgraph_index_status({repositoryId})` once per generation. Verify commit and immutable `spec_id`: configured/capture_complete/complete, eligible = embedded, zero pending/failed/missing-capture/missing-job. Retain exclusions/omissions. Empty queues do not prove readiness. If unavailable, disclose and use exact/lexical/pinned-source evidence; never index as recovery.

Preserve search mode/fallback/truncation and each subject’s pin/evidence. File-card companions/aliases are not relationships. Extractor capabilities and `no_omissions_recorded` do not prove parsing completeness.

## Retain native evidence

Discover **names/schema** only:

```js
text(ALL_TOOLS.filter(x => /mcp__truthgraph_customer__truthgraph_(index_status|search|context|impact_details)$/.test(x.name)).map(x => x.name));
```

Prefer `truthgraph_context` with explicit intent; workflows are equivalent. Use supplied/returned `repo` and `subject`:

```js
const raw = await tools.mcp__truthgraph_customer__truthgraph_context({repositoryId:repo, query:subject, intent:"impact"});
store("tg:impact:raw", raw);
if (raw.isError) { text(raw); exit(); }
const v = raw.structuredContent ?? JSON.parse(raw.content.find(x => x.type === "text").text);
store("tg:impact", v);
const bytes = x => encodeURIComponent(JSON.stringify(x)).replace(/%[0-9A-F]{2}|./g,"x").length;
if (v?.presentation?.view === "compact" && bytes(v) <= 12000) { text(v); exit(); }
const A = x => Array.isArray(x) ? x : [];
const pick = (x, keys) => Object.fromEntries(keys.split(" ").filter(k => x?.[k] !== undefined).map(k => [k,x[k]]));
const d = v?.impact ?? v?.canonical_data ?? v?.context ?? v ?? {}, g = d.graph ?? {};
const summary = v?.impact_summary ?? v?.summary;
const choices = [v?.results,d.impacted_entities,d.items,v?.bundle?.items,v?.operator_answer,g.entities,g.nodes,
  summary && [...A(summary.files),...A(summary.non_file_entities)],v?.runtime_flow?.runtime_evidence];
const rows = choices.find(Array.isArray) ?? [], edges = A(g.edges ?? d.supporting_edges ?? v?.relationships);
const brief = x => {
  x ??= {}; const e = x.entity ?? {}, s = x.match ?? e.metadata ?? x.metadata ?? x;
  const refs = A(x.evidence_refs ?? s.evidence_refs ?? (x.evidence_ref ? [x.evidence_ref] : []));
  return {...pick(x,"subject id reference name family repository path category categories relationships relationship from to impact_class evidence_kind evidence_type confidence confidence_score edge_kind inferred extractor_name"),
    entity:pick(e,"id name family repository"), source:pick(s,"path source_artifact_path source_revision revision_scope start_line end_line source_digest input_digest"),
    evidence_refs:refs.filter(r => typeof r === "string" && r.length <= 300).slice(0,3), evidence_refs_available:refs.length,
    ...(typeof s.excerpt === "string" ? {excerpt_preview:[...s.excerpt].slice(0,300).join(""), excerpt_preview_only:true} : {})};
};
const p = {stored:"tg:impact", selection_scope:"presentation sample; incomplete impact/source", recognized_shape:choices.some(Array.isArray),
  keys:choices.some(Array.isArray) ? undefined : Object.keys(v ?? {}).slice(0,20), status:v?.status ?? d.status, records_available:rows.length, edges_available:edges.length,
  records:rows.slice(0,3).map(brief), edges:edges.slice(0,5).map(brief),
  pin:d.indexed_head ?? d.revision_scope ?? d.pinned_revision ?? v?.bundle?.pinned_revision,
  coverage:d.coverage ?? v?.analysis?.coverage, analysis:pick(v?.analysis,"traversal_complete counts"),
  retrieval:pick(v?.retrieval ?? d.retrieval,"scope truncated traversal_complete has_more next_cursor continuation_request page_limit"),
  delivery:pick(v?.delivery ?? d.delivery,"mode result_id all_details_included summary_complete summary_continuations"),
  discovery:pick(v?.discovery,"requested_mode mode semantic_state phases candidates_truncated source_capture_state"),
  freshness:pick(v?.freshness,"indexed_head current_head source_state verification_scope"),
  source_coverage:pick(v?.source_coverage,"repository_id revision status"), omissions:pick(v?.source_coverage?.omissions,"count bytes pathsTruncated"),
  presentation:pick(v?.presentation,"source_evidence_omitted graph_page_records_omitted"),
  warnings_available:A(v?.warnings).length + A(d.warnings).length, warnings:[...A(v?.warnings),...A(d.warnings)].slice(0,3).map(x => String(x).slice(0,300))};
while (bytes(p) > 12000 && (p.edges.length || p.records.length)) (p.edges.length ? p.edges : p.records).pop();
text(p);
```

Reuse `load("tg:impact")`; keep distinct call/page keys. Review relevant retained edges before paging: skipped evidence will not reappear. Budget graph + source ~16KB. Previews are partial. `full_request.name`/`arguments` re-queries only needed server-omitted source; recheck pins/generation. Other projections reuse stored data. Unknown/errors are not empty success. Python HTTPS cannot replace required native calls. [retrieval.md](references/retrieval.md) covers unusual shapes.

## Expand only missing facts

Reuse evidence/digests. Inventory once, read ranges once; avoid guessed paths/repeated whole files. Verify signatures, control flow, payload rebuilding and dynamic boundaries against pinned source.

Search discovered source roots; initially exclude `*.pb.cc`, `*.pb.h` and identified model/conversation captures. Drill into them for serialization/adapters/fixtures. Do not exclude all tests.

Follow ownership `retrieval.continuation_request` unchanged only for unresolved facts. Retain pages/cursor/scope gaps when stopping. Use immutable impact details:

```js
